# flutter_ai_whisper — Cursor Agent Guide

MCP server that inspects and mutates the state of a running Flutter app over the
Dart VM Service.

**Read `AGENTS.md` first — it is the canonical guide** covering architecture,
the five tools, platform differences, scope and reachability, expression rules,
rebuild semantics, state-management recipes, and the development workflow. This
file adds Cursor-specific notes only.

## Project facts

- Dart CLI speaking MCP on `stdio`. No Flutter dependency.
- `bin/main.dart` registers the tools; handlers live in `lib/tools/`.
- `lib/vm_bridge.dart` owns the VM Service connection and `evaluate`.
- `lib/discovery.dart` finds running apps via the Dart Tooling Daemon.
- `lib/state_discoverer.dart` owns discovery and expression probing.

## Rules that cause real bugs

- Call `connect_to_app` with **no arguments**. It auto-discovers via DTD. Never
  paste the `flutter run` URI — its path is a per-run auth code, stale on every
  relaunch.
- The app URL (`http://localhost:PORT/`) is the static web server, not the VM
  Service. Use the `ws://127.0.0.1:PORT/AUTHCODE=/ws` URI.
- An expression is evaluated in **one** library scope. Visibility follows that
  library's import/export graph, so the wrong choice gives `Undefined name`.
- Private names (`_field`, `_HomePageState`, `_privateMethod`) all fail to
  compile without `libraryUri` pointing at their declaring library.
- Mutating an object does **not** update the view. Plain objects need `setState`
  (mutate inside it); GetX `Rx`, Riverpod, Bloc and `ValueNotifier` self-notify.
- `setState` rebuilds on the **next frame**, not inline — wait a frame, then
  assert against the rendered `Text` widgets, not the variable.
- You can only reach what the object exposes. A getter with no setter cannot be
  assigned, even with perfect injection.
- Flutter Web cannot enumerate state — no `getClassList`, no `dart:mirrors`.
  Pass `expressions` instead, derived from the app's source.
- `CallToolResult.isError` is nullable; `null` means success.

## Verify

```console
dart analyze && dart test
```

## Safety

Executes arbitrary Dart in the app process. Development only — never point it at
a production build or an untrusted app.
